ncept", "title": "metacognition"}], "description": "Students use behaviorist, cognitive, constructivist, and social learning ideas to plan supports."}, {"id": "83ada0f2-0f2a-4bb2-af01-d44dcf3c3bfe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Motivation and engagement", "children": [{"id": "f0ff96a1-9a5a-4aa0-884b-6216ea5d62da", "type": "concept", "title": "self-determination theory"}, {"id": "d57b8b9d-e5e2-4547-8e1e-011d5cb24059", "type": "concept", "title": "goal orientation"}, {"id": "d69e3fab-aa78-496f-b830-676145d4c0dc", "type": "concept", "title": "interest"}, {"id": "45126813-53ec-412b-8aec-d67d6d85917e", "type": "concept", "title": "student agency"}], "description": "Students learn how autonomy, competence, relevance, belonging, and success experiences support cooperation."}]}, {"id": "d8c82a6e-ae13-47ac-8642-2cb2f64b2ef4", "type": "topic", "title": "Building Relationships, Belonging, and Classroom Community", "description": "Strong management is built on relationships that help students feel known, safe, respected, and responsible to one another.", "children": [{"id": "68a7b897-dc4a-4947-8f58-4a42a958b3a6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Teacher-student relationships", "children": [{"id": "022f5a7b-8b0e-45a7-8b58-3218f1babec1", "type": "concept", "title": "greeting routines"}, {"id": "8c605b57-6558-4be1-b337-6f00ed77cae4", "type": "concept", "title": "2x10 strategy"}, {"id": "a14a0b7a-0049-4258-bd1f-1d89237b692d", "type": "concept", "title": "interest inventories"}, {"id": "48119972-0f45-4463-9217-7da94c7f6bef", "type": "concept", "title": "positive contact"}], "description": "Students practice relationship-building moves that support learning and reduce conflict."}, {"id": "682ea060-4957-453c-9c54-514408b96bb9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Peer community", "children": [{"id": "033b822a-28ba-4417-876a-387d294deea8", "type": "concept", "title": "morning meeting"}, {"id": "3290a213-31d2-4e93-8459-b4a212526ac6", "type": "concept", "title": "class agreements"}, {"id": "5b3a